Exceptions and third-party material:

- The gk binary and the reference tool mcref are not part of this folder
  in the gkreasoner repository. In the full dataset, bin/gk and mcref/
  keep the GK licence of the gkreasoner repository, a copy of which is
  bin/LICENSE. The taxonomy data in data/, which parts O6 and O7 read, is
  derived from WordNet 3.0 and is used under the Princeton WordNet
  licence (data/README.md).
- The five Bayesian networks of part O3 (Asia, Earthquake, Cancer,
  Win95pts, Andes) are not included. Part O3 names their source, the
  bnlearn Bayesian network repository, with the download address and the
  SHA-256 of each file. The gk inputs generated from them are included.
- The university inputs of part O3 use the vocabulary of the Univ-Bench
  ontology of the Lehigh University Benchmark (LUBM). Their rules were
  derived from that ontology by tools/extract_univ_bench_rules.py; their
  facts were generated for this paper. The ontology file is not included.
- The inputs of the set "lit" of part O2 restate examples from the
  published literature, from the example programs of plingo, and from
  the public datasets BoardgameQA and defeasible NLI, in gk's input
  language. O2_record/lit_sources.tsv names the source of each input.
- No code of an external system (ProbLog, plingo, clingo, PASTA,
  smProbLog, pgmpy, SPINdle, DEFT, TweetyProject) is included. SYSTEMS.md
  names each system, its version and its source.
